OL,3,GNEWSAFire-damaged school resumes
OL,4,Aclasses in historic house
OL,5,
OL,6,FA primary school that suffered a
OL,7,Fcatastrophic blaze during the summer
OL,8,Fholidays has temporarily resumed
OL,9,Fclasses in an 18th-century country
OL,10,Fhouse.
OL,12,FA fire caused by light refracted off a
OL,13,FPerspex canopy damaged Thomas Bullock
OL,14,FPrimary Academy in Shipdham, near
OL,15,FDereham, Norfolk, on 13 August.
OL,17,FPupils spent seven days learning from
OL,18,Fhome before moving into Letton Hall,
OL,19,Fwhere all 240 pupils are being taught
OL,20,Fin rooms, including the library, dining
OL,21,Fand drawing rooms, while temporary
OL,22,Fclassrooms are built.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
